id: pm-mor9pl
title: Embedded CLI commands fail when an eval host has no script argv entry
description: "The published @unbrained/pm-cli/cli runPmCli(args) entrypoint must accept supplied arguments independently of host process.argv. Node --eval leaves process.argv[1] absent. The internal host-argv reconstruction inserts undefined and command execution reports an untyped slice error; the real public collector control leaves requested telemetry consent unchanged. Normalize the missing script entry while preserving host argv and exit status."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: bugfix,cli,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-13T11:21:09.608Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T12:34:09.626Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-13T12:34:08.593Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-13T12:34:08.593Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: A real Node eval host imports the published CLI wrapper and performs the supplied config mutation without changing host argv or exit status; The identical independent control fails before correction and succeeds after; Packed Node and Bun consumers and unchanged SDK surface and quality gates pass
parent: pm-9rgaal
resolution: Supply a local Commander process prefix through a small argv adapter while preserving host argv and exit status and every existing complexity threshold
expected_result: Supplied public CLI arguments work when an eval host has no script argv entry and pass strict lint
actual_result: "Independent public collector regression,125 focused checks, direct empty-baseline ESLint, typecheck, SDK surface and final9-package Node/Bun/npx/bunx workflows pass; unchanged distribution and40-package runtime budgets pass; revised exact-head hosted static and coverage remain merge prerequisites"
